# OpenSocrates for local Claude Code

OpenSocrates {{PRODUCT_VERSION}} provides the original {{METHOD_COUNT}} canonical
reasoning methods, content revision {{CONTENT_REVISION}}, through one controller.
Use ordinary requests for synthesis, stakeholder context, decisions, and useful
messages. Mechanical work stays light. No additional selector model, automatic
memory enrollment, private transcript reader, or Claude credential copy is used.

## Native package boundary

This profile targets Apple-silicon macOS only. Its manifest is
`.claude-plugin/plugin.json`, hooks are in `hooks/hooks.json`, and the fixed
launcher is `bin/launch.sh`. The runtime is under
`runtime/darwin-arm64/opensocrates-runtime/`. It never resolves from the current
working directory. Windows native Claude delivery is unavailable in this profile;
existing Codex Windows support has a separate package.

Enabled/trusted SessionStart and UserPromptSubmit hooks deliver the bounded
standing entry and complete installed controller/decision-guide locations.
SessionStart after compaction and the next ordinary submission restore entry.
PostCompact is not used for injection because it has no decision control.
Stop and SessionEnd are literal no-ops: there is no read-repair gate, stored
task record, or false application receipt. Malformed, excessive, unknown-event,
or unavailable-runtime input fails open with empty hook output.

The active agent reads complete canonical procedures at materially changed
judgments, using `bin/launch.sh decision claude` or its volatile `--stream`
variant. Full reads, applicability, dependencies, contraindications, stops, and
the grounding audit remain required. Emitted instructions and read assertions
do not prove application or improved outcomes.

## Host trust and evidence

Review the generated manifest and hook commands through Claude's supported
plugin management before enabling. Installation, package generation, and
synthetic probes do not prove live hook delivery. CLI and Desktop local Code
are separate validation cells; cloud, SSH, and WSL are outside this native claim.
Documented Claude hooks: https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks (checked 2026-10-07).

Ordinary Chat and Cowork use a separate content-only account skill export.
Do not upload this native profile there: its top-level executable `bin/` tree
is incompatible with that account-plugin transport. Preserve an existing account
skill until its replacement qualifies and avoid duplicate public controllers.
No application settings or unrelated hooks are owned by the package payload.

